@{
    ViewBag.Title = "Division Maintenance Roster";
    var openWorksheetOnLoad = ((bool)(ViewBag.RosterOpenWorksheet ?? false)) ? "true" : "false";
    Layout = "~/Areas/FRS25/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
    var maintenanceToday = (string)(ViewBag.DivisionMaintenanceToday ?? DateTime.UtcNow.AddMinutes(330).ToString("yyyy-MM-dd", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture));
}
@* Division UI 3.3.0 (view 2.12.0.0) -- six roster items, 16.10.2026:
   1. PRINTED ROSTER carries a Remark column (last recorded visit: outcome, who, when, remark).
      remarkCell() is emitted ONLY when preparePrint asks for it, so the on-screen table is
      byte-for-byte what it was.
   1b. SERVER-SIDE PDF now works. MaintenceRosterPdfController renders this page with ?pdfMode=1
      and waits on window.__rosPdfReady; neither existed here, so that download could only time
      out. The contract is implemented at the foot of the script, with a 120 s ceiling and a
      ready-signal on the failure path so the generator can never block.
   2. SAVE SPINNER clears unconditionally. Both save paths cleared d.saving / S.busy only when
      epoch === S.epoch, so a moved epoch left the Save button disabled reading "Saving visit..."
      for ever. The epoch guard now covers the render only.
   3. STATION PAGINATION states the single-page case explicitly and is never tied to S.busy, plus
      aria-disabled. (Item 2's stuck S.busy was also making the section read as loading.)
   4. ALREADY-ACKNOWLEDGED assets block. `itemOpen === 0` was the only guard and itemOpen is -1
      outside itemMode, so nothing stopped a second acknowledgement on the asset-state path --
      which is why a duplicate save returned the current time: it was a real second visit.
      a.attended now blocks in outcomeDetails AND in the saveOutcome submit handler.
   5. Roster AI "like Alert Analysis" -- NOT in this build; scoped to UI only, awaiting direction.
   *@
@* Division UI 3.2.3 (view 2.11.2.3): the literal at-sign inside the [ROSTER-ACK] console line
   is now doubled. Razor rejects a bare at-sign followed by a space anywhere in a .cshtml,
   including inside a JavaScript string: "A space or line break was encountered after the
   at character". Present since view 2.11.1.0; it only surfaced the first time this file was
   actually served from the IIS path. *@
@* Division UI 3.2.2 (view 2.11.2.3): the Division dropdown no longer lists "Select Division" twice.
   DivisionService.GetAll() prepends its own Id=0 placeholder row, which this view rendered on top of its
   own <option value=""> placeholder; rows with Id <= 0 are now skipped. *@
@* Division UI 3.2.1 (view 2.11.2.1): item-mode save accepts an empty or plain-text CloseItem reply on HTTP 200 and
   logs every reply ([ROSTER-ACK] CloseItem ...). *@
@* Division UI 3.2 (view 2.11.2.0): item mode -- when Roster/MaintenanceState does not return Assets[] (the API on :90
   has no MaintenanceState/CloseAsset and answers with the caller's UserId), attendance comes from each saved finding's
   CloseStatus/ClosedBy and Save closes every open finding through Roster/CloseItem, as the older page did. With an
   upgraded API (Assets[] returned) the evidence-token flow is used again automatically. *@
@* Division UI 3.1 (view 2.11.1.0): dialog side padding; console diagnostics when Save asset acknowledgement is
   disabled ([ROSTER-ACK] lines, incl. the raw Roster/MaintenanceState reply); AI analysis shown as an Alert-Analysis
   style card (confidence ring, coloured verdict, dotted sections); verdict vocabulary fixed (DEFECT LIKELY / WATCH /
   NO DEFECT EVIDENT / INCONCLUSIVE judged on defect evidence only); cause code shown in table, queue, overview, AI card
   and heatmap tooltips. *@
@* Division UI 3.0 (2.10.0.0): reference layout -- side rail (Command centre, Stations, Issues, Asset roster, Outcomes,
   Field worksheet), top bar, lifecycle, station x asset-type heatmap, priority queue, station load, issues by cause and
   recorded outcomes. All views are computed from the already-loaded roster (S.rows + assessed); no new endpoints, no
   sample data. Every 2.11 element id, function and dialog is unchanged. Still pure ASCII, no BOM (see 2.10 below). *@
@* Division UI 2.11 (2.8.11.0): unique asset roster BOUND TO THE SAVED GENERATOR RUN, asset maintenance visits and scoped AI.
   2.11: a blocked acknowledgement names which part of the Roster/MaintenanceState reply is missing, and logs it (tag DIVISION-ACK-TOKEN).
   2.10: THIS FILE IS PURE ASCII ON PURPOSE. It ships without a BOM, and Razor reads a BOM-less view in the server's ANSI code page,
         so a literal dash or middle dot arrives as mojibake. Markup uses numeric entities, script uses \uXXXX. Keep it that way.
   2.9: every AI dialog shows the live stage with elapsed seconds (AiChat step / tool_use frames); a silent request ends after 150 s.
   2.8: track-shorting panel names the roster band and its reason, and binds every scalar fact of an event window.
   2.7: Ask AI bound to the real AiChat/AnalyzeChat contract -- named context keys + roster evidence carried as text messages.
   2.6: Back to worksheet button on a review opened from the station worksheet; a blocked Save names its real reason.
   2.5: no browser re-sweep on load; two-lane request queue so detail tabs and Ask AI are never starved; scope AI reads saved evidence.
   Station worksheets are embedded here; saved asset visits require the maintenance API routes. *@
<style>
#dm { --navy:#112b48; --blue:#2258ba; --teal:#087f79; --red:#b52f3b; --amber:#956015; --ink:#18324d; --muted:#607286; --line:#dce5ee; --bg:#f1f5fa; font:16px/1.5 system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",sans-serif; color:var(--ink); background:var(--bg); border-radius:16px; overflow:hidden; }
